<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $62.9 mln Feb 26.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $62.9 mln Feb 26.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $62.9 million deficit on Feb 26 in the commercial forex market, according to central bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON FEBRUARY 26</p>
<p>Exports: $165.3 million</p>
<p>Imports: $172.4 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $281.1 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $336.9 million</p>
<p>Deficit: $62.9 million</p>
<p>FEBRUARY DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $2.876 million</p>
<p>Imports: $2.907 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $4.280 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $3.315 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $934 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>((-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55 11 248-5418))</p>
</text>
